  "hotelDescription": "Get a fresh perspective on the capital at Premier Inn London City (Old Street). Wake up to amazing views across the London skyline - from the Olympic Park to the Shard - before exploring some of the hidden gems, off-the-beaten-track delights and landmark sights. \n\nDelve into London\u0027s most colourful markets in Spitalfields, around Brick Lane and Petticoat Lane. Catch some cutting-edge performances at the Barbican. Or hop on a tube to explore the West End, St Paul\u0027s Cathedral, the London Eye and more. After a long day or a late night, you\u0027ll find everything you need to relax and recharge: comfy rooms, a top-notch breakfast, and all for a \u0027pinch yourself\u0027 price.",
  "hotelDirections": "Leave \u0027Old Street\u0027 Tube Station (Northern Line) by Subway 1, (City Road North). As you exit take the steps to your left, walk straight ahead along the footpath (City Road) with the row of shops and cafes on your right hand side. You will pass two small roads on your right. Continue until you reach the second corner, where the \u0027Three Crowns\u0027 Public House is located. Walk past this pub and cross the pedestrian crossing on your right (Silicon Way), where the hotel entrance is situated. No onsite parking is available.",
